WEBVTT

voice-01-1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.600 line:0
Over a weekend, the feed is held for days without an update.

voice-01-2
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.700 line:0
So the vault keeps the exchange's hours.

voice-02-1
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.200 line:0
Maat's agent runs on Claude, and only proposes.

voice-03-1
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.200 line:0
On Basescan, a refusal reads Success.

voice-04-1
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:31.200 line:0
This is the owner's own treasury, and the vault holds its limits: per trade, per day, per stock.

voice-04-2
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.100 line:0
Maat's agent cannot move them.

voice-05-1
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.900 line:0
Change one word of the rationale, and the hash stops matching.

voice-06-1
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.200 line:0
You need not take our word for it.

voice-07-1
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.900 line:0
The exchange was shut for Thanksgiving.

voice-08-1
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.500 line:0
On a market holiday, the vault refuses every trade.

voice-09-1
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.600 line:0
Friday: an early close.

voice-10-1
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:05.500 line:0
Two probes asked the vault that day: allowed before the close, refused after.

voice-11-1
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.100 line:0
A brief is a short public message on Base.

voice-12-1
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.700 line:0
Maat's agent can be persuaded.

voice-12-2
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:19.600 line:0
The vault cannot: whatever a brief talks it into is weighed by the same rules.

voice-13-1
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.200 line:0
Each address is public. Read it yourself.

voice-14-1
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.500 line:0
The tests run in the open.

voice-15-1
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.800 line:0
Zero is shown as zero.

voice-16-1
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.300 line:0
Maat. Every trade is weighed.
